2024-11-19T11:18:05 |From fd848f0d43b843c66aaf43c2861ba8e31cebc1e8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
2024-11-19T11:18:05 |From: bluhm <bluhm@openbsd.org>
2024-11-19T11:18:06 |Date: Sat, 8 Jul 2023 14:49:55 +0000
2024-11-19T11:18:06 |Subject: [PATCH] Fix Perl tests in OpenBSD regress.
2024-11-19T11:18:06 |
2024-11-19T11:18:06 |Disable Perl test t/porting/exec-bit.t as it only checks permissions.
2024-11-19T11:18:07 |The x-bit in OpenBSD CVS tree does not match Perl distribution tar.
2024-11-19T11:18:07 |This is known and accepted.
2024-11-19T11:18:07 |
2024-11-19T11:18:07 |Set permission of Test-Harness source.sh and source_args.sh to
2024-11-19T11:18:08 |executable as Perl uses it to test module features. Stay close to
2024-11-19T11:18:08 |upstream. During regress, set the x-bit of the files in obj
2024-11-19T11:18:08 |directory. Do not touch src tree, it might be read-only.
2024-11-19T11:18:09 |
2024-11-19T11:18:09 |discussed with anton@; OK afresh1@
